        "title": "About Migration Crisis",
        "subject": "Migration Crisis",
        "summary": "This event concerns an episode of heightened irregular crossings into Ceuta, the Spanish autonomous city on the North African coast that borders Morocco. Such episodes sit within the wider Western Mediterranean migration route, where border management, access to asylum procedures, bilateral Spain–Morocco cooperation, and the safety of people attempting crossings are recurring issues.",
        "facts": [
          {
            "label": "Location and status",
            "value": "Ceuta is a Spanish autonomous city; its autonomy is governed by Organic Law 1/1995. Its land boundary with Morocco is an external border of the Schengen area.",
