              "o2"
            ]
          },
          {
            "label": "Migration-route context",
            "value": "The EU describes the Western Mediterranean route as irregular arrivals to Spain by sea and by land through Ceuta and Melilla; people commonly transit through Morocco or Algeria on this route.",
            "source_ids": [
